WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
 Today, more than half the world’s poorest

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.940
 people live in sub-Saharan Africa.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:05.860
 Why?

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.760
 Why is it that most of Africa stays poor,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.720
 while other parts of the world prosper?

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.900
 People have lots of theories.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.860
 Clean water is simply hard to find.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.020
 The present day problems of the African continent

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.760
 are tied to its colonial history.

00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:22.800
 But I say Magatte Wade’s explanation

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.400
 makes the most sense.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.700
 African governments simply have too many rules.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.900
 Once you hire someone

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.480
 good luck getting rid of them for any reason.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.760
 Then there’s taxes.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.579
 The tax code is so complicated.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.000
 Some people say it's worth at least two

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.380
 or three truckloads of paper.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.340
 Wade started this lip balm company in Senegal.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.820
 Some ingredients she needs are not made there,

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.080
 so she imports them,

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.000
 but the government makes that expensive.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.800
 Some of them have a 70 percent import tariff on them.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.620
 So it almost doubles the prices.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.580
 Exactly.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.700
 Many people, then escape the tax by paying bribes.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.820
 We hear about African corruption.

00:00:58.829 --> 00:00:59.940
 People complain about corruption as

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.480
 if corruption is a root problem I say no --

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.820
 Corruption is also a natural consequence

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.530
 of stupid senseless idiot laws.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.060
 There’d be just as much corruption in America

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.520
 if we had these rules?

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.540
 Absolutely.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.060
 The only way to fix corruption is to simplify.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.980
 Wade’s business survived because she was

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.260
 fortunate to find a helpful bureaucrat.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.100
 I went to see the Head of Customs

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.650
 and we started looking together.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.270
 He didn’t demand a bribe.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.400
 We found a clause in one of the binders saying

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.700
 actually if you're exporting at least 80 percent

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.080
 of your products and if you've been in business

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.150
 for two years then you can ask for an exemption.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.320
 You survive through a loophole but that takes

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.490
 connections and time

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:47.460
 Exactly. Exactly.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.040
 I imagine the leaders of these countries

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.160
 mostly mean well.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.720
 They see how damaging this is.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.780
 Why do they impose all these rules?

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.770
 I am not so sure all of them get it.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.970
 Look at the UN Sustainable Development Goals.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.100
 The UN’s development goals includes things

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.470
 like “Inclusive and equitable education,

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:10.640
 climate change, and gender equality.”

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.120
 There is no mention of rules that kill business.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.700
 We have chains around our necks.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.440
 No one is seeing it.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.800
 And then they want to come talk to me about inequality.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.780
 We need greater economic freedom.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.180
 Simple rules that everyone can understand.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.040
 Yes. Yes.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:29.420
 That diagnosis is known by almost no one.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.940
 It should be known!

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.840
 If you just look at the rest of the world

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.380
 you can see what’s worked and what hasn’t.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.740
 Wade just made this movie about that.

00:02:37.749 --> 00:02:39.960
 Why is it that a couple decades ago you know

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.080
 China was at the same level as most African countries?

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.920
 Countries like Singapore made it.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.380
 Countries like Hong Kong made it.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.880
 Even a place like Dubai

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.940
 bare land of sand, desert sand

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.500
 and all of a sudden within 12, 15 years,

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.600
 Dubai – one of the financial centers of the world -

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.740
 and you’re like what?

00:02:57.749 --> 00:02:59.260
 What happened here?

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.620
 They understood if we do not work hard to

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.659
 make it easy for businesses to set up and

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:09.810
 be ran no businesses is going to come

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.760
 But international aid organizations

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.020
 have a different solution.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.000
 They say the nations of the world

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.020
 need to send more help.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:21.200
 Governments already send $50 billion a year to Africa.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.880
 And companies promote themselves by donating.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.760
 What if I start a shoe company,

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.300
 and every time I sold a pair of shoes,

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.840
 I gave a pair away.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.440
 These kids’ll have shoes for the rest of their life.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.520
 Tom’s shoes has donated 93 million pairs of shoes.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.700
 Do you know that we have two hundred thirty-two

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.999
 hundred thirty-two shoe making small businesses

00:03:42.999 --> 00:03:46.499
 each one of them hiring directly at least 15 people

00:03:46.499 --> 00:03:47.739
 In this little village.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:48.260
 Yes.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.140
 So when you buy your shoes in the US

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.020
 and pairs of shoes are being put in a container

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.440
 to be shipped over to my village.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.280
 Shoemaker has now to close the doors because

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.080
 who can compete against free?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.609
 This man is still in business, but it’s a struggle.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.200
 I know it came from a good place.

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:13.249
 I get it.

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:15.940
 But can you just think further down the road

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.420
 unless you think that we really sincerely

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.560
 have nothing including even shoemakers!

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.280
 And I think that's terrible!

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:26.540
 To give in such a way that has no end

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.900
 Yet Tom’s Shoes two-for-one deal is popular.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.440
 One company started it did so well with it.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.880
 With a buy one we're going to give one

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.500
 for free to poor people.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.060
 But now you're seeing it with tampons

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:37.960
 you're seeing it with soap,

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.300
 you're seeing it with everything.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.820
 It would be better, says Wade,

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.200
 if westerners encouraged African governments

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.320
 to stop strangling their own entrepreneurs.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.280
 If I have a job then, guess what?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.920
 My malnutrition problem goes poof!

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.560
 My even access to clean water goes poof.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.660
 You know it just poof, poof, poof!

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.100
 But without jobs, millions risk their lives

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.130
 trying to get to richer countries.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.400
 Some of my most entrepreneurial people

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.620
 who are right now serving us fish food

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.940
 at the bottom of the ocean

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.200
 because there is not enough jobs

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.590
 and why there is not enough jobs?

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.800
 Because the business climate sucks so much

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.300
 that people like me can't do that work

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.080
 of creating companies and jobs.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.940
 Many of those deaths would be prevented

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:24.980
 if Africa just didn’t have so many dumb rules.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:28.000
 And that's what inequality we should talk about.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.460
 No one talks about it.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.160
 An equal playing field of rules.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.280
 Yes.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.280
 Yes.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:38.260
 Let's create greater economic freedom

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:42.420
 in all countries so that all people everywhere

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.060
 get a chance to free enterprise.

